values ('ap_chemistry', 7, '7.8', array['7.8']::text[], 'diagram', 'Particulate model of a reversible reaction', 'A particulate diagram shows the relative numbers of reactant and product particles before and at equilibrium, and from these the value of the equilibrium constant.', '[{"label": "Prior to equilibrium", "meaning": "Relative numbers of reactant and product particles in the initial mixture."}, {"label": "At equilibrium", "meaning": "Relative numbers of reactant and product particles present once the forward and reverse rates are equal."}, {"label": "Equilibrium constant", "meaning": "K is found from the particle counts at equilibrium, using the same form as the K expression."}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=task0067-chem-u5-u9-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_chemistry-u7-r2-005; ced=7.8.A.1 "Particulate representations can be used to describe the relative numbers of reactant and product particles present prior to and at equilibrium, and the value of the equilibrium constant"')
